            <ArticleTitle>Occlusion of coronary vein grafts secondary to non-penetrating chest injury.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>362-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Eighteen months after graft surgery to the posterior descending, circumflex, and left anterior descending coronary arteries, it seems that blunt chest trauma caused by a car accident resulted in occlusion of the grafts.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
